#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Understand open-shell versus closed-shell options and the effect on subspace"
" construction for the latest version of Sample-based quantum diagonalization"
" (SQD)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Understand open-shell versus closed-shell options and the effect on subspace"
" construction"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/select-open-"
"closed-shell.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this guide, we will show how to choose subspace dimensions in the "
"`qiskit_addon_sqd` package to post-process quantum samples using the [self-"
"consistent configuration recovery "
"technique](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.05068).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"More importantly, this guide also highlights some differences in the "
"behavior in the subspace construction when run in `open_shell = False` or "
"`open_shell = True` modes:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`open_shell = False` only works when the number of spin-up and spin-down "
"electrons is the same.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`open_shell = True` must be used when the number of spin-up and spin-down "
"electrons is different. It can also be used when the number of spin-up and "
"spin-down electrons is the same. However, in this last case, there is a "
"difference in the sizes of the subspaces generated between `open_shell = "
"False` and `open_shell = True`, as discussed in this guide.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**NOTE:** Some of the electronic-configuration (bitstring) manipulations in "
"this package have as a goal to preserve the total spin symmetry $S^2$. "
"Standard Selected Configuration Interaction (SCI) solvers cannot impose "
"$S^2$ conservation exactly. Consequently, they do so approximately via a "
"Lagrange multiplier.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The choice of electronic configurations entering the eigenstate solver can "
"also have a strong effect in the conservation of spin. For example, in a "
"(2-electron, 2-orbital) system, one can sample the configuration "
"$|1001\\rangle$ (having a single spin-up excitation over the RHF state "
"$|0101\\rangle$), which is a linear combination of the open-shell singlet "
"and triplet states, respectively $(|1001\\rangle ± |0110\\rangle) "
"/\\sqrt{2}$. If the configuration |0110⟩ is not sampled, one can construct "
"neither eigenfunction of total spin, leading to spin contamination or "
"redundancy (the configuration |1001⟩ is involved in a CI calculation, but "
"has coefficient 0 in the CI vector). Given that a single sample "
"$|1001\\rangle$ is generated in the quantum computer, this is how the `sqd` "
"package handles this situation:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`open_shell = False`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The $1001$ bitstring is split in half, representing spin-up and spin-down "
"configurations: $10$ (up) and $01$ (down).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The list of unique spin-polarized configurations is constructed: "
"$\\mathcal{U} = [01, 10]$.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We then consider all possible combinations of $\\mathcal{U}$ elements to "
"form the basis: $\\left \\{ |0101\\rangle, |0110\\rangle , |1001\\rangle , "
"|1010\\rangle \\right \\}$, which contains the singlet and triplet states.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`open_shell = True`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Contrary to the `open_shell = False` case, we do not combine the halves of "
"the bitstring to form the basis.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Closed-shell {#closed-shell}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This example shows how the bitstrings are manipulated in a (2-electron, "
"4-orbital) system.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Specify by hand a dictionary of measurement outcomes:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Transform the counts `dict` into a bitstring matrix and probability array "
"for post-processing:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Subsample a single batch of size two:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"``n_batches = 1``: Number of batches of configurations used by the different"
" calls to the eigenstate solver\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"``samples_per_batch = 2``: Number of unique configurations to include in "
"each batch\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Obtain decimal representation of the spin-up and spin-down bitstrings used "
"by the eigenstate solver.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first element in the tuple corresponds to the decimal representation of "
"the spin-up configurations, while the second element in the tuple "
"corresponds to the decimal representation of the spin-down configurations:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that while the number of samples per batch is two, and the sampled bitstrings are: $00010010$ and $01001000$, four electronic configurations are generated per spin-species. In this case, the set of unique spin-polarized configurations is given by:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{U} = \\{ 0001, 0010, 0100, 1000 \\}\n"
"$$\n"
"whose base-10 decimal representation is\n"
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{U}_{10} = \\{ 1, 2, 4, 8 \\}\n"
"$$\n"
"Basis of the subspace:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The eigenstate solver takes all possible pairs of spin-up and spin-down "
"bitstrings to construct the basis $\\mathcal{B}$ of the subspace:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 1: $|00010001\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 2: $|00010010\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 3: $|00010100\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 4: $|00011000\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 5: $|00100001\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 6: $|00100010\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 7: $|00100100\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 8: $|00101000\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 9: $|01000001\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 10: $|01000010\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 11: $|01000100\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 12: $|01001000\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 13: $|10000001\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 14: $|10000010\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 15: $|10000100\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 16: $|10001000\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The subspace dimension is upper-bounded by**:  $2 \\cdot$ "
"(`samples_per_batch`)$^2$.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Open-shell {#open-shell}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we specify that `open_shell = True`, we do not include all unique half-bitstrings as spin-up and spin-down configurations, thus yielding a smaller basis than when specifying `open_shell = False`.\n"
"Basis of the subspace:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 1: $|00010010\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 2: $|00011000\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 3: $|01000010\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Element 4: $|01001000\\rangle$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The subspace dimension is upper-bounded by**:  "
"(`samples_per_batch`)$^2$.\n"
msgstr ""
